# Copy to client/.env for local overrides. You almost certainly do not need it.
#
# Leave VITE_API_URL unset and the app calls a relative /api, which is what you
# want everywhere:
#
#   - in development, vite.config.js proxies /api and /uploads to localhost:5000
#   - in production, vercel.json rewrites them to the deployed API
#
# Both mean the browser only ever talks to one origin, so CORS cannot break the
# site and no API address is baked into the build. Moving the server later is a
# one-line change to vercel.json, not a rebuild.
#
# Set this ONLY to point a build at an API that is not proxied - say, a local
# client against a staging server. It replaces the base URL outright, so it has
# to include the /api path:
#
#   right:  https://checkwise-api.onrender.com/api
#   wrong:  https://checkwise-api.onrender.com
#
# Setting it on a host that already rewrites /api is the usual way to reintroduce
# the CORS failures the proxy exists to prevent.
VITE_API_URL=
